 base='# Structured-overlap meta-learning in a Linear SRN\n\n'+verdict+' '+('Confirmation uses14 paired seeds; the six-seed screen is separate.' if stage=='confirm' else 'Neither candidate qualified; confirmation was stopped by the registered rule.')+'\n\n'
 base+='The question was whether organizing shared and conflicting sequence examples within a task creates stronger context-specific learning of the identical target sequence while retaining Mixed and unpracticed-C transfer. The capacity preflight passed24/24 two-exception task–initialization cases (required20); all72 pilot cases completed330 updates. This establishes fixed-family learnability with sufficient practice, not20-update inner-loop competence.\n\n'
 base+='## Fixed experiment\n\nTwenty original P2-independent Transfer FOMAML episode960 models and their actual outer Adam moments were loaded. The eight-unit identity recurrence is evaluated manually, despite the unused tanh flag in its nn.RNN container. There are172 prediction parameters in six tensors, including separately trained input/recurrent biases, plus two reset inner-only policy parameters. No new centering or normalization was applied to the inherited weights. The original source initialization contract was retained; no architecture change or episode10000 checkpoints were used.\n\nEach episode has two independent-reset eight-symbol paths, seven teacher-forced predictions per subtrial. The generator conditionally enforces different first tokens, consistent full-prefix labels, compatible ordered context contrasts, exact source exclusions and genuine exceptions at prediction5/6. This is a restricted, demonstrably learnable family; it is not an unrestricted random task family. The two potential exceptions share an ordered class contrast. Later positions after divergent histories are neither additional critical cells nor valid shared-Q cells. All masks and rejected-generation counts are archived.\n\n'
 base+='Each X10/Y10 inner update processes both subtrials, averages14 prediction cells, and uses the original CE+.2 detached-confidence execution objective, Adam.005 and jointclip1. Fresh policy/inner Adam and h0 reset prevent cross-trial carry. All three physical cue columns can be practiced during pretraining; Q is unpracticed within that episode.\n\n'
 base+='At inner10, query X; at inner20, query both familiar contexts and Q. With critical mask M and full-prefix-and-target-shared mask V,\n\n`L_early = mean CE_X(θ10)`\n\n`L_fam = .75 mean CE_XY(θ20) + .25 mean_M CE_XY(θ20)` when M is nonempty; otherwise `L_fam = mean CE_XY(θ20)`. Missing critical CE is NaN, never zero.\n\n`L_Q = mean_V CE_Q(θ20)`; index V before cross-entropy.\n\n`g = .2 ∇θ10 L_early + .5 ∇θ20 L_fam + .3 ∇θ20 L_Q`.\n\nThese are detached first-order gradients mapped to the initialization; no inner-optimizer Jacobian, component normalization or policy outer update. Clip the combined gradient once at1, then take one outer Adam.001 update with inherited moments.\n\n'
 base+='A has zero/one/two exceptions in50/0/50% of episodes; B in25/50/25%; C in50/40/10%. Same family/roles/alternatives are paired across arms. A/B match total exceptions and eligible/critical cells over480-episode blocks; C intentionally has fewer exceptions and more eligible Q cells. Raw query passes/examples match. **The conditional critical term is active in50/75/50% of episodes**, yielding expected outer critical-mixture masses .0625/.09375/.0625. Thus A/B do not isolate structural organization from effective critical-loss allocation. This coupling was recorded before meta-training and was not corrected by changing the requested objective. Existing P2 episodes already had a shared prefix; the new manipulation is multiple-example organization plus this explicit compound objective.\n\n'
 base+='## Screening and untouched-seed confirmation\n\n'+(OUT/'SCREENING_DECISION.md').read_text().replace('# Screening decision','')+'\n\nScreen:18×480 episodes. '+('Confirmation:28×960 episodes, endpoints+480/+960, no intermediate selection. ' if stage=='confirm' else '')+'Every continuation starts the original960 source, never a screening/pilot-adapted model. Target adaptation is the unchanged single seven-token sequence with330A10/B10 updates, original Adam/policy contract, and bitwise fixed C column. Full331 states and six physical cues are retained. Corrected-v2 held-out diagnostic libraries are globally excluded from new meta paths; pilot and benchmark paths are also excluded. Source+0 targets and diagnostic branches are reused exactly once per seed.\n\n'
 base+='## Numerical outcomes\n\n'+endpoints.to_markdown(index=False,floatfmt='.6g')+'\n\nCE is nats. Strong familiar means each A/B CE≤.5 and accuracy≥6/7; strict C means CE≤.1, perfect7/7 and gap≤.1; original C/Mixed-both success uses CE≤.5 and accuracy≥6/7. Original functional splitting uses the unmodified predecessor criterion, including its late-floor constraints. The original gate can fail despite positive earlier specificity.\n\nCandidate-minus-A paired effects, complete planned seeds,10,000 whole-seed resamples; pointwise95% intervals:\n\n'+pc.to_markdown(index=False,floatfmt='.6g')+'\n\nMean and median effects, individual-seed signs and raw values are preserved. A confidence interval spanning zero establishes neither equivalence nor preserved performance. No tasks, positions, transitions or directions are resampled as networks. No screening seeds are pooled with confirmation.\n\n'
 base+='The first-block measures are signed: `D_A=(L_A0−L_A10)−(L_B0−L_B10)` and `D_B=(L_B10−L_B20)−(L_A10−L_A20)`, with frozen same-weight A/B losses at each state. Raw own/cross gains, starting losses, floor flags, both directional raw and baseline-adjusted switch costs, restored-Adam diagnostics, original endpoint gates, fixed matched-acquisition bins and unavailable-bin statuses are in the tables. Positive context specificity is functional evidence at that learning period; it does not establish persistent separate memory stores. Late near-zero losses cannot establish shared learning.\n\n'
 base+='## Figures\n\n'+''.join(f'![Figure {i}](figures/{"" if stage=="confirm" else "screen_"}figure_{i}.png)\n\n' for i in [1,2,3])+'Figure1 uses actual practiced pre-update loss (blueA/orangeB), all seeds and seed-bootstrap intervals, preserving switch jumps; first100 and first20 views accompany it. Figure2 shows frozen six-cue CE over all330 updates and first120. Figure3 links seed IDs across C-gap versus first-block learning and reserved conflict accuracy; * marks familiar-qualified, + marks Mixed-both success. Supplements show signed own/cross gains, switch costs, restored-Adam effects, geometry, matched bins and mechanism decomposition.\n\n'
 base+='## Exact linear explanation and limitations\n\nAt time t, `h_t = R h_(t−1) + W_x x_t + W_c c + b`, with h0=0, so `z_t(c)=z_t(0)+K_t W_c c`, where `K_t=W_o sum_(j=0)^(t−1)R^j`. Set `z0=z(0)`, `u=(zA+zB)/2−z0`, `v=(zA−zB)/2`. Then `zA=z0+u+v`, `zB=z0+u−v`, `zMixed-average=z0+u`, `zC=z0+K_t wC`; `zC−(zA+zB)/2=K_t(wC−(wA+wB)/2)`. At fixed t and weights the context contribution is independent of token history. Separate bias tensors sum into b mathematically but remain separately optimized.\n\nAll four raw/centered class logits, norms and margins are retained by position. Double-geometry identities and separately bounded float32 native replay are checked in the archived mathematical tables. Mixed-average is an interpolation and obeys the familiar CE convexity bound; Mixed-both is a different physical cue. C has a nonzero learned input column here, unlike earlier zero-third-channel Linear experiments. Its column is frozen during target practice. This affine explanation is not a hidden-state rescue or proof of natural memory retrieval; centroid/PCA distances and larger vector norms are not evidence of separate learning or causal mediation.\n\nThe comparison manipulates a compound training ecology, not human prior experience in isolation. Unselected B has no confirmation result; this experiment does not refute the general importance of structured experience. Strong target transfer may coexist with weak reserved conflict learning. Teacher-forced seven-position prediction does not test free-running motor execution. Restricted generator feasibility, two pilot initializations,14 confirmation seeds, pointwise intervals, floor effects, missing matched bins and screened candidate choice limit generalization. No unsuccessful/null outcome justifies tuning.\n\n'
 base+='## Integrity and stopping\n\nActual new scientific optimizer steps (including the separate pilot): '+str(budget['scientific_optimizer_steps'])+'; breakdown: `'+json.dumps(budget['breakdown'],sort_keys=True)+'`. Separate implementation fixtures:162 inner+8 outer=170 updates. Saved audits check all source hashes, masks, query states/gradients, Adam continuation, target C freezing, four-class probabilities, all331 states, diagnostic resets/labels and source-code immutability. Paired block/switch/C/update-diagnostic trajectories are in `tables/*_paired_intervals.csv` and `*_paired_seeds.csv`, with complete seed resampling at each fixed checkpoint. Expected RED failures and corrected analysis-import, audit-receipt naming pytest-collection and export-dependency failures remain in `audit/`. Scientific training stopped at the registered budget. No tuning, additional architecture, rescue search or further training is authorized by reproduction.\n'
