 hand='# Researcher handoff\n\n'+verdict+'\n\nTeach-back: we asked whether practicing shared and context-specific examples together changes how a small Linear SRN subsequently learns the same target sequence under A and B, while retaining C/Mixed transfer. Each inner update saw two reset sequence examples. We measured X after10 updates, familiar and shared-prefix-only Q after20, combined three first-order gradients, and updated the initialization once. Screening froze '+str(cand)+' before14 untouched seeds were run. Strong transfer alone is not the target outcome; it must accompany stronger functional A/B-specific learning than referenceA.\n\n'+endpoints[endpoints.dose.eq(last)].to_markdown(index=False,floatfmt='.6g')+'\n\nRead `REPORT.md` for actual paired intervals and qualification of every claim. All signs and seed IDs remain in `tables/*paired_seed_effects.csv`; negative/absent bins are never converted to zero. The first-block specificity is own minus cross CE gain, not hidden distance. Switching costs use same weights; late CE floors can conceal continued specialization. C is a learned third cue during pretraining and never practiced during target training. Linear cue effects are additive and history independent at each position.\n\nThe capacity pilot proves this registered family can be learned within330 updates from two fixed source models; it does not prove inner20 success. The new family is constrained to avoid inconsistent labels and opposing context preferences. B also receives greater effective critical-loss mass than A, despite equal total exceptions. Do not describe this as an isolated structure-only mechanism. Existing P2 tasks already had shared prefixes.\n\nStart with Figure1 first20, Figure2, and Figure3; then inspect signed own/cross, floors, matched bins, conflict correct/wrong cue advantage and the exact decomposition. Use `REPRODUCIBILITY.md` for hashes/table-only plots. Do not rerun training, change thresholds or overwrite sealed data. Any new scientific test needs a new fixed protocol and version.\n'
 (OUT/'RESEARCHER_HANDOFF.md').write_text(clean_prose(hand))
 audit='# Implementation audit\n\nFrozen source/reuse audit: `audit/source_audit.json`; original sources and checkpoint SHA256: `registry/sources.csv`; complete parent dependency chain: `registry/parent_hashes.json`. Original PRD and pre-outcome protocol: `docs/structured_overlap_meta/PRD.md`, `registry/PREREGISTRATION.md`. Append-only implementation decisions: `SCRATCHPAD.md`.\n\nStrict RED→GREEN logs cover generator/exclusions/masks, two-subtrial objective, independent early/final gradient reference, capacity gate, matched streams, pilot resets, retained numerical failures, query schedules/weights, selection, paired referenceA, recurrence replay, component history, budgets, sealed plotting and hash tampering. Log31 records a missing statistics import,39 records refused receipt overwrite after the expanded numerical checks,53 records duplicate test-name collection errors;69 records an export requested before its analysis registry existed. Corrections use explicit source imports, a versioned receipt importlib collection and explicitly sequenced table export. Original logs remain. Font-cache warnings affect plotting cache only.\n\nImplementation fixture totals are162 inner and8 outer steps. The final pure suite excludes optimizer-producing reference fixtures already run;31 predecessor regressions exclude only the documented optimizer fixtures. Scientific updates are fully counted separately; no scientific run was retried or dropped.\n\n'+pd.DataFrame([budget['breakdown']]).to_markdown(index=False)+'\n\n`verify.py` independently reconstructs h0-reset Linear trajectories and BPTT gradients from saved states, with original fixed tolerances. It checks earlyAdam10/finalAdam20 and every outer transition from step960. `pilot_verify.py` checks all72×331 model/policy/optimizer states, all667,296 position records, original initializations and withheld cue columns. `diagnostic_checks.py` checks registered correct/wrong labels, allfour probabilities, fresh states,20-step histories and final metrics. `final_checks.py` checks exact grids, unchanged source scientific code, candidate-minus-A arithmetic, baseline bitwise reuse and frozen selection chronology. These audits perform zero optimizer updates and no native replay of matched branches.\n\nFull generated libraries, raw trajectories, mathematical identities, component gradients and optimizer checkpoints are retained. A trained source/model is the statistical unit; tasks/positions are averaged within seed before inference. Source+0 branches stay in their archived namespaces. No source checkpoint, sealed predecessor artifact or ignore rule was changed.\n'
 (OUT/'IMPLEMENTATION_AUDIT.md').write_text(clean_prose(audit))
